IMPORT prelude

§ `Codex Insurance Limited — accident & sickness hospitalization policy`

§§ `Fact schema (verbatim, inputs/schema.md) — DECLAREs`

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF Sickness, `Accidental injury`, Neither

DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
  Skydiving, `Military service`, Firefighting, `Police service`, Other

DECLARE Claim
  HAS `agreement signed`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `premium paid month`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `hospitalization month`                      IS A NUMBER
      `hospitalization ground`                     IS A Ground
      `age at hospitalization`                     IS A NUMBER
      `causes`                                     IS A LIST OF Cause
      `fraud month`                                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `misrepresentation month`                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit month`                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `written confirmation month`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `dispute arisen`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable to settle month`                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `arbitration commenced month`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `valid arbitration award issued`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `written proof of claim month`               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `recovery sought month`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `policy term months`                         IS A NUMBER

§§ `Supporting helpers (verbatim, inputs/schema.md) — call, do not redefine`

GIVEN  `event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
       `limit month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no later than` MEANS
  CONSIDER `event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m AT MOST `limit month`

GIVEN  cs IS A LIST OF Cause
       c  IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arose out of` MEANS elem c cs

§ `Coverage logic`

§§ `§1.1 — the hospitalization must be for sickness or accidental injury`

-- "The payment of any benefit under this policy is conditioned on the policy being
-- in effect at the time of the hospitalization for sickness or accidental injury
-- on which the claim for such benefit is premised."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `hospitalization ground`
    WHEN Neither THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `§1.1(1)-(2) — agreement signed, premium paid`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`premium paid by the time of hospitalization` claim MEANS
    `no later than` (claim's `premium paid month`) (claim's `hospitalization month`)

§§ `§1.3 — wellness-visit disclosure condition, and §1.1(3)'s "still pending" excuse`

-- "No later than the 7th month anniversary of the effective date of this policy, you
-- will supply us with written confirmation from the medical provider in question of a
-- wellness visit for yourself with a qualified medical provider occurring no later
-- than the 6th month anniversary of the effective date of this policy."
--
-- §1.1(3) treats this condition as satisfied while it is "still pending" (no
-- confirmation has been supplied yet, but the 7-month deadline for supplying one has
-- not yet passed as of the hospitalization) as well as when it has been "satisfied in
-- a timely fashion" (a confirmation was supplied on time, of a visit that itself
-- happened on time, with a qualified provider). Only a LATE confirmation, or a missed
-- deadline with none supplied at all, fails it.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim, w IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 1.3 satisfied given confirmation supplied at` claim w MEANS
        w AT MOST 7
    AND `no later than` (claim's `wellness visit month`) 6
    AND claim's `wellness visit provider qualified`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 1.3 condition met or still pending` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `written confirmation month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN claim's `hospitalization month` AT MOST 7
    WHEN JUST w THEN `section 1.3 satisfied given confirmation supplied at` claim w

§§ `§1.2 — cancelation for fraud, misrepresentation, or material withholding`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`cancelled for fraud or misrepresentation` claim MEANS
        isJust (claim's `fraud month`)
    OR  isJust (claim's `misrepresentation month`)

§§ `§1.2 / §3.6 — automatic cancelation at the end of the one-year policy term`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization within the policy term` claim MEANS
    claim's `hospitalization month` AT MOST claim's `policy term months`

§§ `§1.1 — the policy is "in effect" at the time of the hospitalization`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy in effect at hospitalization` claim MEANS
        claim's `agreement signed`
    AND `premium paid by the time of hospitalization` claim
    AND `section 1.3 condition met or still pending` claim
    AND NOT (`cancelled for fraud or misrepresentation` claim)
    AND `hospitalization within the policy term` claim

§§ `§2.1 — general exclusions`

-- "Your policy will not apply to, and no benefit will be paid with respect to, any
-- event causing sickness or accidental injury arising directly or indirectly out of:
-- 1. Skydiving; or 2. Service in the military; or 3. Service as a fire fighter; or
-- 4. Service in the police; or 5. [age at the time of the hospitalization >= 80]."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`event excluded` claim MEANS
        `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Skydiving
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Military service`
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Firefighting
    OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Police service`
    OR  claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

§§ `§3.2.1 — arbitration as a condition precedent to liability`

-- "... such arbitration to be commenced within three (3) months from the day such
-- parties are unable to settle the dispute or difference. If You fail to commence
-- arbitration in accordance with this clause, it is agreed that any cause of action
-- and any right to make a claim ... shall be extinguished completely."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration commenced within three months of impasse` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `unable to settle month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST m THEN `no later than` (claim's `arbitration commenced month`) (m PLUS 3)

-- "Where there is a dispute or disagreement, the issuance of a valid arbitration
-- award shall also be a condition precedent to our liability under this Policy."
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration condition when disputed` claim MEANS
        `arbitration commenced within three months of impasse` claim
    AND claim's `valid arbitration award issued`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration preconditions satisfied` claim MEANS
    IF claim's `dispute arisen`
    THEN `arbitration condition when disputed` claim
    ELSE TRUE

§§ `§3.2.1 — sixty-day waiting period before seeking recovery`

-- "In no case shall You seek to recover on this Policy before the expiration of
-- sixty (60) days after written proof of claim has been submitted to Us in
-- accordance with the provisions of this Policy."
-- The Claim schema tracks time in whole months, not days; 60 days is treated here
-- as 2 months (60 / 30). This clause is read as unconditional (it applies "in no
-- case", not only when a dispute has arisen).
GIVEN claim IS A Claim, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`recovery timing satisfied given proof of claim at` claim p MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `recovery sought month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST r THEN r AT LEAST (p PLUS 2)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`recovery not sought before the sixty-day wait ends` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `written proof of claim month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST p THEN `recovery timing satisfied given proof of claim at` claim p

§ `Top-level decision`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
covered claim MEANS
        `hospitalization is for sickness or accidental injury` claim
    AND `policy in effect at hospitalization` claim
    AND NOT (`event excluded` claim)
    AND `arbitration preconditions satisfied` claim
    AND `recovery not sought before the sixty-day wait ends` claim
